      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-30_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
        <p>Makharoff to the supreme command of the fleet, and General Kuropatkin to the head oif the land foxes in the Fa; East. The latter was, it was widely known, a bitter opponent to the Viceroy at headquarters. To each was given absolutely independent command with the power to report direct to the Tsar;_ and thus Admiral Alexeieff automatically became a mere figurehead. Now, to crown all, Admiral Skrydloff, another prominent opponent of Admiral Alexeieff and his policy, has been gazetted to the command of the remnant of the Russian fleet, irrespec- tive of the Viceroy, who was not consulted,</p>
